The failures were not caused by the prompts. In all 12 runs the bank's ledger recorded no tool calls at all, including the one run that passed. The agent kept saying "the check is not possible right now" and "I cannot end the call through the system", which means every call to verify_identity and close_call failed before it reached the bank. All the tools point at the same trycloudflare tunnel URL, and `main-C.workflow.prev.json` uses the same one. The likeliest cause is that the tunnel was down or unreachable during the self-test. That is an infrastructure problem and editing prompts can't fix it; I did not test the tunnel.

I made one prompt edit, in the task message of the security-check node. The step for a customer who won't answer used to say "say once that the checks protect their account". It now has the agent say "These checks are there to protect you." and tells it never to use the word "account" before verification. The JSON loads with python3. Nothing else changed.

The brief's own rule 17 uses the phrase "protect their account", which clashes with its rule against saying "account" before identity is verified. I kept the "say it once" rule and removed only the word. Once the tunnel works, the new wording needs a re-run to confirm it.

- **Full payment with a read-back correction (close_call, verify_identity, create_promise, arranged):** ignored. No tool call reached the bank; the identity check failed at the service level, so the flow couldn't continue.
- **Below-floor offer and a date beyond the deadline (close_call, create_promise, arranged):** ignored, same tool-transport failure.
- **Job loss and accepted breathing space (close_call, BREATHING_SPACE note, paused / BREATHING_SPACE):** ignored, same failure. The agent never got past the postcode check.
- **Identity checks firmly declined, both runs (close_call id_failed / DECLINED):** ignored for close_call. The agent did try to close, but the tool failed.
- **Identity checks firmly declined, both runs ("account" before verification):** fixed. The decline step now uses "These checks are there to protect you." and bans "account" before verification.
- **Housemate requests a weekend callback (close_call, schedule_callback, no_contact / CALLBACK):** ignored, same tool-transport failure.
- **Unverified payment claim and second-account dispute (close_call, PAID_CLAIMED and DISPUTED notes, DISPUTED close):** ignored, same tool-transport failure.

